# PersonalCRM — Rules for Codex 5.2 (Cursor)

## Source of truth
1) OpenAPI contract: /openapi/personalcrm_openapi_v1.yaml
2) Postgres schema: /db/personalcrm_postgres_schema_draft.sql

Any change to endpoints or payloads MUST start by updating the contracts, then code.
Never "invent" fields or endpoints that are not in the contracts.

## Multi-tenancy
- Every request is scoped by `workspace_id` (query param per OpenAPI).
- All DB queries MUST filter by workspace_id AND deleted_at IS NULL unless explicitly needed.

## Assistant access & privacy
- Records have `visibility`: private/shared/limited.
- Assistant must not see or edit private_notes, trust_score, emotional_balance, etc. unless they have explicit permission.
- Implement server-side redaction (do not rely on frontend).

## Soft delete
- Delete operations set deleted_at; never physically delete in normal flows.

## Pagination
- Cursor-based pagination only (limit + cursor -> next_cursor).
- Cursor must be opaque (base64 JSON), stable, and include tie-breaker fields.

## Quality bar
- Provide integration tests for each router: list/create/get/update/delete.
- Add DB indexes ONLY if justified by actual query patterns.
- Keep handlers thin; put logic in services.

## Git discipline
- One PR per epic.
- Keep contract changes and implementation in the same PR.
- Update README if developer workflow changes.
